      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This preliminary study in 20 patients demonstrated that ultrasonic coronary angioplasty in the setting of bypass grafting is feasible, safe, and able to recanalize atherosclerotic vessels. Shorter monorail probes were superior to longer probes without guidewires in terms of success of vessel recanalization; >95% of particle debris was <25 microm in size."},
